{
  "about": "Ruling 58's camera evaluation: the labels template, one entry per expected photograph (c01 to c12). labels.json is written from it and the owner's descriptions, and committed before any model is shown the set.",
  "conventions": "file: the photograph in bench/camera/. original: the phone's file name. shows: what it shows, in the owner's description. set: sensitive or ordinary. handwritten: true or false. angled: no, slight, or yes. expected_gate: hold (as sensitive or as unsure) or clear. ocr_keywords: words on the material, spelled normally, that the OCR should recover (a misspelled word on the card is not chosen, so an OCR miss on it is not counted against the OCR). expected_tasks: for a commitment, each expected task as match (groups of words, lower case; a written task matches when every word of any one group is in it) and project (one of the courier's seven, or unsorted). scene: commitment or reference; null for a sensitive photograph, which should not reach the scene. scene_unsure_accepted: true where the label-writer accepts unsure from the model as a reasonable answer, recorded as such; the label stands.",
